    "probe_text": "Here is the exact ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, read from the OfficeFloor pipeline at `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` and its function classes. There is **no** Spring `@RestController` for owners \u2014 creation is handled entirely by the pipeline.\n\n## Gates that run before anything is built\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Denial \u2192 `AuthorizationDeniedException` \u2192 **403**.\n2. **Idempotency short-circuit** (`CheckIdempotencyKey`) \u2014 reads optional `Idempotency-Key` header. If the key was seen before, it takes the *replay* branch (`RespondWithReplayedOwner`): re-loads the original owner and returns it **200** (no 201, no Location), skipping every step below. A missing/unknown key proceeds to create.\n\n## Create path (all steps below run under one `transaction` governance, committed once at the end)\n\n3. **Bean validation of the request DTO** (`BuildOwner`, the single `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` binder). Constraint failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400**. Constraints:\n   - `firstName` / `lastName`: `@NotNull`, name `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull @Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull @Pattern(\"^[-0-9+() ]*$\") @Size(1..20)`\n   - `email`: `@Email @Size(max 255)` (optional); `postcode`: `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")` (optional); `title`/`address`/`addressLine1`/`addressLine2` sizes (optional)\n\nThen, in `BuildOwner`'s method body, in order:\n4. **Telephone normalization** \u2014 `E164.normalize(...)` \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 **400**.\n5. **Address resolution** \u2014 `AddressForm.apply(...)` (prefers `addressLine1/2`, else flat `address`, rejects if neither) \u2192 `AddressRequiredException` \u2192 **400**.\n6. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (side-effect: object construction via `OwnerMapper`).\n7. **Future registration-date check** \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` \u2192 **400**.\n8. **Registration-date defaulting + business-day roll-forward** (side-effect: defaults to today if null, then advances past weekends/2026 holidays); publishes `sharesHousehold` flag.\n\nThen the ensure-chain (each reads the built `Owner`):\n9. **Disposable-email check** (`EnsureOwnerEmailNotDisposable`) \u2014 blocklist mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail \u2192 `DisposableEmailException` \u2192 **400**.\n10. **Postcode-within-region check** (`EnsureOwnerPostcodeWithinRegion`) \u2014 NSW/VIC/QLD ranges \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` \u2192 **400**.\n11. **Identity-uniqueness check** (`EnsureOwnerIdentityUnique`) \u2014 scans `findAll()`, skips soft-deleted, compares full `IdentityKey` \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 **409**.\n12. **City-capacity check** (`EnsureOwnerCityWithinCapacity`) \u2014 normalized-city count `>= 50` \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409**. (Does *not* exclude soft-deleted.)\n13. **Daily-limit check** (`EnsureDailyOwnerLimitNotExceeded`) \u2014 same-registration-date count `>= 100` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` \u2192 **429**. (Does *not* exclude soft-deleted.)\n\nThen the mutating/persisting steps:\n14. **Assign customer code** (`AssignOwnerCustomerCode`) \u2014 side-effect: sets `customerCode = <REGION>V2<FY2><SHA256-hash8><Luhn>`.\n15. **Deduplicate customer code** (`DeduplicateOwnerCustomerCode`) \u2014 side-effect: appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 until unique among existing codes.\n16. **Persist** (`SaveOwner`) \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)`. The real DB write.\n17. **Record idempotency key** (`RecordIdempotencyKey`) \u2014 side-effect: if header present, `idempotencyStore.record(key, owner.getId())` (putIfAbsent).\n18. **Respond** (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) \u2014 side-effects: computes derived DTO fields (namesakeCount, membershipPoints/level capped, bulkSignupWarning, possibleDuplicate\u2026), writes **AUDIT + NOTIFY log entries**, and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- Step order is deliberate: validation (3\u20135) runs before load/uniqueness so a bad body is 400 rather than being masked.\n- The soft-delete exclusion is **inconsistent** \u2014 the identity check (11) skips soft-deleted owners, but the city-capacity (12) and daily-limit (13) counts do **not**. Worth confirming that's intended.\n- Entity-level constraints on `Owner` (`@NotEmpty address/city/telephone`, E.164 `@Pattern`) are *not* the `@Valid` trigger here \u2014 only the DTO is validated in the pipeline; those would only surface at JPA persist time.\n- `DataIntegrityViolationException` is mapped to **404**, not 409/400 \u2014 looks like a possible bug in the escalation handler.\n\nI read the code without changing anything."
